Let $R$ be a ring with unity and let $a$ be a von Neumann regular element of $R$. Then the following hold 
\begin{enumerate}
	\item $a$  is unit-regular  $\Longleftrightarrow a^{+}$ is unit regular for some and hence all reflexive inverses $a^{+}$ of $a$. 
\end{enumerate}

\label{thm:canfell}
The following statements are equivalent for a ring $R$.	\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
		\item If $Ra+ann_l(b)=R$ for $a,b\in R$, then there exists a unit $u\in U(R)$ such that $a-u\in ann_l(b)$.
		\item $R$ is left uniquely generated (left UG).
	\item If $Ra=Rb$ for $a,b\in R$, then $a=vb$ for some left unit $v\in R$.
		\end{enumerate}

{\label{ASouter}}
	Let $R$ be an exchange ring. Then for any element $a \in R$, 
\[	\{b : Ra + \operatorname{ann}_\ell(b) = R\} \,\, = \,\,  \bigcup_{x \in T(a)} xR\]
